+# Platform-Guardian Delta — Pages Deploy Drift at T+32h, F-12 Closure
+
+**Cycle**: 2026-10-29 11:45+08, Job 477792, role: platform-guardian
+**Tracking issue**: #2431 (open until operator redeploy)
+**Baseline**: guardian pass PANEL B in #1946 (2026-10-28) — "stable skew, not
+propagation; fix is one operator redeploy, no repo PR can reach it"
+**Method**: zero-side-effect read-only GETs against both studio edges and the
+production gateway. No deploys triggered, no writes, no credentials.
+
+## PANEL B delta — the skew persisted through the full window
+
+The 32-hour question this delta answers is whether the Pages skew documented
+yesterday was propagation lag or an unmaintained deploy. The answer is now
+unambiguous: **unmaintained**. Three independent measurements agree.
+
+First, the entry asset. Pages still serves `index-CAV1C5sl` — the byte-for-byte
+same hash #1946 recorded yesterday — while Vercel's entry moved from
+`index-DWg5blwL` to `index-DspHVcxo`. An unchanged content hash across a
+window in which the sibling edge moved forward is the signature of a deploy
+that was never retriggered, not of a slow CDN.
+
+Second, the SW asset plane. Pages `/sw-assets.json` still returns the 6364-byte
+SPA-fallback HTML document (the exact artifact size #1946 recorded), meaning
+the manifest request still falls through to the SPA shell and the service
+worker still receives HTML where it expects JSON. Pages `/sw.js` remains the
+stale 4188-byte v4 build with the pre-#1761 hex-only cache regex and empty
+PRECACHE_URLS. Vercel, by contrast, serves a real manifest that has itself
+changed size (1852B → 1929B), proving the manifest pipeline is healthy on an
+edge that gets redeployed.
+
+Third, the consequence stands and compounds: users landing on the Pages cohort
+continue to get zero offline resilience and a service worker whose cache
+validation cannot match Vite's base64url asset hashes. The drift is no longer
+"yesterday's anomaly" — it is the studio's steady state on one of its two
+production edges, and the cohort assignment between Pages and Vercel is not
+something the repo controls. The fix remains exactly what #1946 concluded: one
+operator redeploy of the Cloudflare Pages project. Verification is a single
+GET — `pages.dev/sw-assets.json` must stop returning the HTML fallback.
+
+This delta deliberately does not re-classify severity or propose new mechanics;
+it adds the dated evidence trail that was missing. #1946 noted "no open WO
+tracked Pages staleness" — that gap is now closed by issue #2431, which stays
+open until the operator action lands.
+
+## PANEL A-lite — production gateway healthy; F-12 verified closed
+
+The gateway's real host answered `/healthz` 200 (`status:"healthy"`,
+`chat_ready:true`) and `/readyz` 200 with a fresh timestamp; the
+`x-render-routing` header check was clean on the suffixed host. One deliberate
+addition to yesterday's panel: the **F-12 CORS preflight finding from #2355 is
+empirically closed**. An `OPTIONS /healthz` preflight carrying Origin
+`https://supremeai-studio.pages.dev` now returns 200 with the correct
+`access-control-allow-origin` echo and the full method list — the allow-list at
+`gateway/service/app.py:271` (which includes both studio edges) is live on
+production. #2332 corrected the attribution of that finding; this probe closes
+the loop with a live result.
+
+Tower remained functional throughout the cycle (session handshake, tool
+surface listing, and queue reads all clean), and the loop client now surfaces
+the tower-board/P0-darkness line honestly on gh-less runtimes — first observed
+this cycle, consistent with R61's option-B lane from #2318.
+
+## Disclosure
+
+Total live calls this cycle: 8 read-only GETs/OPTIONS (3 Pages, 3 Vercel, 2
+gateway) plus Tower session reads. Zero deploys triggered, zero state mutated,
+no credentials used, no load beyond single sequential requests.
